1
00:00:01,540 --> 00:00:03,180
Hello again.

2
00:00:03,880 --> 00:00:07,100
What do you think you can see behind me?

3
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:13,460
Looks like a giant concrete structure.

4
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:18,040
However, this is one of Wrocław’s symbols.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,320
This place is called the Hall of the Century,

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,060
Hala Stulecia.

7
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:26,580
It was built in 1913

8
00:00:26,580 --> 00:00:29,700
by the architect Max Berg.

9
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:35,640
Back then, to build such a huge structure made of concrete

10
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:39,600
was a very courageous, groundbreaking idea.

11
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:42,320
In the year 2006,

12
00:00:42,820 --> 00:00:48,520
this place was added to the UNESCO Heritage List.

13
00:00:50,040 --> 00:00:52,760
Today, it is not just a frozen museum.

14
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:56,900
The place actually hosts performances,

15
00:00:57,940 --> 00:01:02,360
exhibitions, music shows, sports events, etc.

16
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:07,460
I invite you to walk around this amazing geometrical structure

17
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:10,780
and also visit the inside of the structure.

18
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:12,940
See you on our next stop.

19
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:14,160
Do widzenia!
